[1m[38;5;231mWhich approach should the design use?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: namespaced global (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246midentity.js as a classic script exposing AppIdentity. Works from file:// and http, keeps the record shape in one [39m
     [38;5;246mplace, testable in Node.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: ES modules
     [38;5;246mCleanest boundary, but commits to http serving and needs .mjs juggling to avoid breaking the CommonJS src/ [39m
     [38;5;246mdirectory.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: bare storage convention
     [38;5;246mNo new file; each consumer reads the sessionStorage key directly. Least code now, but duplicates the record shape [39m
